{"task_id": "Mbpp/4", "solution": "import heapq\n\ndef heap_queue_largest(numbers: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n largest integers from a list using a heap-based approach,\n    returning them in descending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Use heapq.nlargest to efficiently get the n largest elements.\n    # This returns elements in ascending order.\n    largest_elements = heapq.nlargest(n, numbers)\n\n    # Sort the result in descending order as required.\n    largest_elements.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    return largest_elements"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/6", "solution": "def differ_At_One_Bit_Pos(num1: int, num2: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if two numbers differ at exactly one bit position.\n    This is true if their XOR result is a power of two.\n    \"\"\"\n    xor_result = num1 ^ num2\n    # A number differs at one bit position if the XOR result is a positive power of 2.\n    # A positive integer N is a power of 2 if N > 0 and (N & (N - 1)) == 0.\n    return xor_result > 0 and (xor_result & (xor_result - 1)) == 0"}
