{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "def _find_first_occurrence(s: str, char: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of a character in a string.\"\"\"\n    for i in range(len(s)):\n        if s[i] == char:\n            return i\n    return -1\n\ndef _find_last_occurrence(s: str, char: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of a character in a string.\"\"\"\n    for i in range(len(s) - 1, -1, -1):\n        if s[i] == char:\n            return i\n    return -1\n\ndef _remove_characters_at_positions(s: str, positions: list[int]) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Removes characters from a string at the specified indices.\"\"\"\n    if not s or not positions:\n        return s\n\n    # Convert positions to a set for O(1) average time complexity lookup\n    positions_to_remove = set(positions)\n    result_chars = []\n    for i, char_s in enumerate(s):\n        if i not in positions_to_remove:\n            result_chars.append(char_s)\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n\ndef remove_Occ(input_string: str, character: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes the first and last occurrence of a given character from the string.\n    assert remove_Occ(\"hello\",\"l\") == \"heo\"\n    \"\"\"\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(input_string, character)\n\n    if first_idx == -1:\n        # Character not found, return original string\n        return input_string\n\n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(input_string, character)\n\n    positions_to_remove = []\n    if first_idx == last_idx:\n        # Only one occurrence of the character\n        positions_to_remove.append(first_idx)\n    else:\n        # Two distinct occurrences\n        positions_to_remove.append(first_idx)\n        positions_to_remove.append(last_idx)\n\n    return _remove_characters_at_positions(input_string, positions_to_remove)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/11", "solution": "def _find_first_occurrence(string: str, char: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Find first occurrence of character. Returns -1 if not found.\"\"\"\n    return string.find(char)\n\ndef _find_last_occurrence(string: str, char: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Find last occurrence of character. Returns -1 if not found.\"\"\"\n    return string.rfind(char)\n\ndef _remove_characters_at_positions(string: str, positions: list) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Remove characters at specified positions.\"\"\"\n    if not positions:\n        return string\n\n    positions_to_remove = set(positions)\n    \n    result = []\n    for i, char_at_idx in enumerate(string):\n        if i not in positions_to_remove:\n            result.append(char_at_idx)\n    return \"\".join(result)\n\ndef remove_Occ(input_string: str, character: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Remove first and last occurrence of a given character from the string.\"\"\"\n    first_idx = _find_first_occurrence(input_string, character)\n    \n    if first_idx == -1:\n        # Character not found at all\n        return input_string\n    \n    last_idx = _find_last_occurrence(input_string, character)\n\n    if first_idx == last_idx:\n        # Only one occurrence of the character\n        return _remove_characters_at_positions(input_string, [first_idx])\n    else:\n        # Two or more occurrences, remove both first and last\n        return _remove_characters_at_positions(input_string, [first_idx, last_idx])"}
