{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "def count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of substrings where the sum of their digits equals their length.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(s)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        current_sum = 0\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            # Calculate the sum of digits for the current substring s[i:j+1]\n            current_sum += int(s[j])\n            \n            # The length of the current substring is (j - i + 1)\n            current_length = j - i + 1\n\n            if current_sum == current_length:\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/61", "solution": "def count_Substrings(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Count substrings where the sum of digits equals their length.\n    Iterates through all substrings, calculates digit sum, and compares to length.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    n = len(s)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i, n):\n            substring = s[i:j+1]\n            digit_sum = sum(int(char) for char in substring)\n            if digit_sum == len(substring):\n                count += 1\n    return count"}
