{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Bell number, representing the number of ways to partition a set of n elements.\n    It uses a dynamic programming approach based on the Bell triangle.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize with B_0\n    bell_row = [1] \n\n    # Iterate to build the Bell triangle up to n rows\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        next_bell_row = [bell_row[-1]]  # The first element of the new row is the last of the previous\n        for j in range(i):\n            # Each subsequent element is the sum of the element to its left in the current row\n            # and the element above it in the previous row.\n            next_bell_row.append(next_bell_row[-1] + bell_row[j])\n        bell_row = next_bell_row\n    \n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row (0-indexed).\n    return bell_row[0]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "```python\ndef is_Monotonic(arr: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given array is monotonic (non-decreasing or non-increasing).\n    An empty array or an array with one element is considered monotonic.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(arr) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    is_non_decreasing = True\n    is_non_increasing = True\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        if arr[i] < arr[i-1]:\n            is_non_decreasing = False\n        if arr[i] > arr[i-1]:\n            is_non_increasing = False\n    \n    return is_non_decreasing or is_non_increasing\n```"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/67", "solution": "def bell_number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Bell number B(n), representing the number of ways to partition\n    a set of n labeled elements into non-empty, non-overlapping subsets.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # dp[i][j] will store the Stirling number of the second kind S(i, j),\n    # which is the number of ways to partition a set of i elements into j non-empty subsets.\n    dp = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case for Stirling numbers of the second kind: S(0, 0) = 1\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the dp table using the recurrence relation: S(i, j) = S(i-1, j-1) + j * S(i-1, j)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            if j == i:\n                dp[i][j] = 1  # S(i, i) = 1\n            else:\n                dp[i][j] = dp[i-1][j-1] + j * dp[i-1][j]\n\n    # The Bell number B(n) is the sum of Stirling numbers of the second kind for a given n:\n    # B(n) = sum_{k=0 to n} S(n, k)\n    bell_n = 0\n    for k in range(n + 1):\n        bell_n += dp[n][k]\n\n    return bell_n"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/68", "solution": "def is_Monotonic(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the array is monotonic (either non-decreasing or non-increasing).\n    An array with less than 2 elements is considered monotonic.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array) < 2:\n        return True\n\n    is_non_decreasing = True\n    is_non_increasing = True\n\n    for i in range(1, len(array)):\n        if array[i] < array[i-1]:\n            is_non_decreasing = False\n        if array[i] > array[i-1]:\n            is_non_increasing = False\n            \n    return is_non_decreasing or is_non_increasing"}
