{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "def comb_sort(lst: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements using the comb sort algorithm in ascending order.\n    Returns a new sorted list, preserving the original input.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(lst)\n    arr_copy = list(lst)  # Create a copy to preserve the original list\n\n    gap = n\n    swapped = True\n\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        # Calculate the next gap value\n        gap = int(gap / 1.3)\n        if gap < 1:\n            gap = 1\n\n        swapped = False\n        # Compare all elements with current gap\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if arr_copy[i] > arr_copy[i + gap]:\n                arr_copy[i], arr_copy[i + gap] = arr_copy[i + gap], arr_copy[i]\n                swapped = True\n\n    return arr_copy"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/71", "solution": "def comb_sort(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements using the Comb Sort algorithm.\n    Returns a new list with elements sorted in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    working_list = list(input_list)  # Create a mutable copy to avoid modifying the original list\n    n = len(working_list)\n\n    GAP_REDUCTION_FACTOR = 1.3  # Optimal gap reduction factor\n\n    gap = n\n    swapped = True\n\n    # Continue sorting until the gap is 1 and no swaps occur in a pass\n    while gap > 1 or swapped:\n        # Calculate the next gap value\n        gap = int(gap / GAP_REDUCTION_FACTOR)\n        if gap < 1:\n            gap = 1  # Ensure gap is at least 1 for the final pass (bubble sort)\n\n        swapped = False  # Reset swapped flag for the current pass\n\n        # Perform a \"bubble\" pass with the current gap\n        for i in range(n - gap):\n            if working_list[i] > working_list[i + gap]:\n                # Swap elements if they are in the wrong order\n                working_list[i], working_list[i + gap] = working_list[i + gap], working_list[i]\n                swapped = True  # Mark that a swap occurred in this pass\n\n    return working_list"}
