{"task_id": "Mbpp/75", "solution": "def find_tuples(tuple_list: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds tuples where all elements are divisible by k from a list of tuples.\n    This function processes a list of tuples and returns only those tuples\n    where every element is perfectly divisible by the given integer k.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_divisible(element: int, k: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if a single element is divisible by k.\n        Returns True if element % k is 0, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        return element % k == 0\n\n    def _check_tuple_divisibility(tuple_data: tuple, k: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if all elements in a given tuple are divisible by k.\n        It iterates through the tuple, using _is_divisible for each element.\n        \"\"\"\n        return all(_is_divisible(element, k) for element in tuple_data)\n\n    # The main function logic\n    result_tuples = []\n    for current_tuple in tuple_list:\n        if _check_tuple_divisibility(current_tuple, k):\n            result_tuples.append(current_tuple)\n    return result_tuples"}
