{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n    Uses dynamic programming to build the sequence iteratively.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1 or n == 2:\n        return 1\n\n    # dp array to store sequence values, using 1-based indexing for convenience\n    dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n    dp[1] = 1\n    dp[2] = 1\n\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        dp[i] = dp[dp[i - 1]] + dp[i - dp[i - 1]]\n\n    return dp[n]"}
