{"task_id": "Mbpp/100", "solution": "def next_smallest_palindrome(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the next smallest palindrome greater than the specified integer.\n    It iteratively increments the input number until a palindrome is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _reverse_number(num: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Helper to reverse the digits of a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n        reversed_num = 0\n        temp = num\n        while temp > 0:\n            digit = temp % 10\n            reversed_num = reversed_num * 10 + digit\n            temp //= 10\n        return reversed_num\n\n    def _is_palindrome(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Helper to check if a non-negative integer is a palindrome.\"\"\"\n        if num < 0:  # Palindromes are generally considered non-negative.\n            return False\n        return num == _reverse_number(num)\n\n    current_num = n + 1\n    while True:\n        if _is_palindrome(current_num):\n            return current_num\n        current_num += 1"}
