{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number A(n, m) using a recursive approach with memoization.\n    A(n, m) is the number of permutations of {1, ..., n} with exactly m ascents.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {}\n\n    def _compute_eulerian_recursive(n_val: int, m_val: int) -> int:\n        # Base Cases\n        if n_val == 0:\n            return 1 if m_val == 0 else 0\n        \n        # Eulerian numbers A(n,m) are non-zero only for 0 <= m <= n-1\n        if m_val < 0 or m_val >= n_val:\n            return 0\n        \n        # A(n,0) = 1 for n > 0\n        if m_val == 0:\n            return 1\n        \n        # A(n, n-1) = 1 for n > 0\n        if m_val == n_val - 1:\n            return 1\n\n        # Check memoization table\n        if (n_val, m_val) in memo:\n            return memo[(n_val, m_val)]\n\n        # Recurrence Relation: A(n, m) = (m + 1) * A(n-1, m) + (n - m) * A(n-1, m-1)\n        result = ((m_val + 1) * _compute_eulerian_recursive(n_val - 1, m_val) +\n                  (n_val - m_val) * _compute_eulerian_recursive(n_val - 1, m_val - 1))\n        \n        memo[(n_val, m_val)] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _compute_eulerian_recursive(n, m)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the Eulerian number A(n, m) using the standard sum formula.\n    This function expects non-negative integer inputs for n and m.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Helper function for binomial coefficient C(N, K)\n    def combinations(N, K):\n        if K < 0 or K > N:\n            return 0\n        if K == 0 or K == N:\n            return 1\n        if K > N // 2:\n            K = N - K  # Optimization: C(N, K) = C(N, N-K)\n        \n        res = 1\n        for i in range(K):\n            res = res * (N - i) // (i + 1)\n        return res\n\n    # Eulerian number A(n, m) is defined as the sum:\n    # A(n, m) = sum_{k=0 to m} ((-1)^k * C(n+1, k) * (m - k + 1)^n)\n    \n    eulerian = 0\n    for k in range(m + 1):\n        term = ((-1)**k) * combinations(n + 1, k) * ((m - k + 1)**n)\n        eulerian += term\n        \n    return eulerian"}
