{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, rotation_count: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of times a rotated binary string's decimal equivalent is odd.\n    Performs left rotations on the string for the given number of times.\n    \"\"\"\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_string = binary_string\n\n    for _ in range(rotation_count):\n        # Convert the current binary string to its decimal equivalent.\n        decimal_value = int(current_string, 2)\n        \n        # Check if the decimal value is odd.\n        if decimal_value % 2 != 0:\n            odd_count += 1\n            \n        # Perform a left rotation: move the first character to the end.\n        current_string = current_string[1:] + current_string[0]\n            \n    return odd_count"}
