{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "solution": "```python\ndef search(array: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the element that appears exactly once in a sorted array.\n    Uses binary search for O(log n) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n\n        # Adjust mid to be an even index.\n        # This ensures mid points to the start of a potential pair (idx, idx+1).\n        if mid % 2 == 1:\n            mid -= 1\n\n        # If array[mid] and array[mid+1] form a pair,\n        # the unique element must be in the right half of the array.\n        if array[mid] == array[mid + 1]:\n            low = mid + 2\n        # Otherwise, array[mid] is either the unique element or\n        # the unique element is in the left half, breaking the pair pattern.\n        else:\n            high = mid\n\n    return array[low]\n```"}
