{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def amicable_numbers_sum(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sums all amicable numbers up to the specified limit.\n    It identifies amicable pairs by calculating sums of proper divisors.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def sum_proper_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a given number.\"\"\"\n        if n <= 1:\n            return 0\n        s = 1  # 1 is always a proper divisor\n        for i in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                s += i\n                if i * i != n:\n                    s += n // i\n        return s\n\n    found_amicable = set()\n    \n    for a in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if a in found_amicable:\n            continue\n\n        sum_a = sum_proper_divisors(a)\n\n        # Check if sum_a is within the limit and forms an amicable pair with 'a'\n        # sum_a > a to avoid double-counting pairs and exclude perfect numbers (where sum_a == a)\n        if sum_a > a and sum_a <= limit:\n            sum_b = sum_proper_divisors(sum_a)\n            if sum_b == a:\n                found_amicable.add(a)\n                found_amicable.add(sum_a)\n\n    return sum(found_amicable)"}
