{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def _count_zeros(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of zero values in an array.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for x in arr:\n        if x == 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\ndef _count_non_zeros(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of non-zero values in an array.\"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    for x in arr:\n        if x != 0:\n            count += 1\n    return count\n\ndef _calculate_ratio(zeros: int, non_zeros: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zeros to non-zeros.\"\"\"\n    if non_zeros == 0:\n        # As per design, \"Undefined behavior for edge cases (no non-zero values)\"\n        # Simple division will raise ZeroDivisionError which fulfills this.\n        return float('inf') if zeros > 0 else 0.0 # Or allow ZeroDivisionError\n    return zeros / non_zeros\n\ndef zero_count(arr: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes in an array of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    zeroes = _count_zeros(arr)\n    non_zeroes = _count_non_zeros(arr)\n    ratio = _calculate_ratio(zeroes, non_zeroes)\n    return ratio"}
