{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(array: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes in an array of integers.\n    Handles division by zero gracefully, returning appropriate float values (e.g., infinity or NaN).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def count_zeros(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of zero values in the array.\"\"\"\n        return arr.count(0)\n\n    def count_non_zeros(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of non-zero values in the array.\"\"\"\n        return len(arr) - count_zeros(arr)\n\n    def calculate_ratio(zeros: int, non_zeros: int) -> float:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zeroes to non-zeroes, handling division by zero.\"\"\"\n        if non_zeros == 0:\n            if zeros == 0:\n                return float('nan') # 0/0 case\n            else:\n                return float('inf') # x/0 where x > 0\n        return float(zeros) / non_zeros\n\n    num_zeros = count_zeros(array)\n    num_non_zeros = count_non_zeros(array)\n\n    return calculate_ratio(num_zeros, num_non_zeros)"}
