{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def flip(arr, k):\n    \"\"\"Reverses elements from index 0 to k-1 in the list.\"\"\"\n    start = 0\n    end = k - 1\n    while start < end:\n        arr[start], arr[end] = arr[end], arr[start]\n        start += 1\n        end -= 1\n    return arr\n\ndef find_max_index(arr, n):\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element in the first n elements of the list.\"\"\"\n    max_val = arr[0]\n    max_idx = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if arr[i] > max_val:\n            max_val = arr[i]\n            max_idx = i\n    return max_idx\n\ndef pancake_sort(arr):\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements in ascending order using the pancake sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n <= 1:\n        return arr[:]\n\n    current_arr = list(arr)\n\n    # Start from the complete list and reduce the size of the unsorted part\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find the index of the maximum element in the current unsorted part\n        max_idx = find_max_index(current_arr, curr_size)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at the end of the current unsorted part\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # If the maximum element is not at the beginning, flip to bring it to index 0\n            if max_idx != 0:\n                flip(current_arr, max_idx + 1)\n\n            # Flip the entire unsorted part to move the maximum element to its correct position\n            flip(current_arr, curr_size)\n\n    return current_arr"}
