{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "def find_max_index(arr: list, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element in arr[0...n-1].\"\"\"\n    max_idx = 0\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if arr[i] > arr[max_idx]:\n            max_idx = i\n    return max_idx\n\ndef flip(arr: list, i: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Returns a new list with elements from index 0 to i reversed.\"\"\"\n    segment_to_flip = arr[0 : i + 1]\n    segment_to_flip.reverse()\n    \n    # Construct the new list by combining the flipped segment and the rest\n    new_arr = segment_to_flip + arr[i + 1 :]\n    return new_arr\n\ndef pancake_sort(arr: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements using the pancake sort algorithm.\"\"\"\n    working_list = list(arr) # Create a working copy to preserve original list\n    n = len(working_list)\n\n    # Iterate from the full list size down to 2\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        # Find index of the maximum element in the current unsorted segment\n        max_idx = find_max_index(working_list, curr_size)\n\n        # If the maximum element is not already at its correct sorted position\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            # Move the maximum element to the beginning of the list if it's not already there\n            if max_idx != 0:\n                working_list = flip(working_list, max_idx)\n            \n            # Move the maximum element from the beginning to its correct sorted position\n            working_list = flip(working_list, curr_size - 1)\n            \n    return working_list"}
