{"task_id": "Mbpp/166", "solution": "def find_even_pair(numbers: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of pairs of integers in a list that xor to an even number.\n    Orchestrates pair generation, XOR calculation, and evenness checks.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def generate_pairs(nums: list[int]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n        \"\"\"Generates all unique pairs from distinct positions in the input list.\"\"\"\n        pairs = []\n        n = len(nums)\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                pairs.append((nums[i], nums[j]))\n        return pairs\n\n    def calculate_xor(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the bitwise XOR of two integers.\"\"\"\n        return a ^ b\n\n    def is_even(value: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Determines if an integer is an even number.\"\"\"\n        return value % 2 == 0\n\n    def count_even_pairs(pairs_list: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts how many pairs in a list have an even XOR result.\"\"\"\n        even_xor_count = 0\n        for num1, num2 in pairs_list:\n            xor_result = calculate_xor(num1, num2)\n            if is_even(xor_result):\n                even_xor_count += 1\n        return even_xor_count\n\n    all_pairs = generate_pairs(numbers)\n    result_count = count_even_pairs(all_pairs)\n    return result_count"}
