{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(sorted_array, n, element):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Calculate the threshold for majority\n    threshold = n / 2.0\n\n    # Count occurrences of the element in the sorted array\n    # Since the array is sorted, this count is accurate.\n    count = sorted_array.count(element)\n\n    # Return True if the count exceeds the threshold\n    return count > threshold"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "def is_majority(array: list, n: int, element: any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if an element is the majority element in a sorted array.\n    The majority element occurs more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    def _find_first_occurrence(arr, target, low, high):\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the first occurrence of the target using binary search.\"\"\"\n        first_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                first_idx = mid\n                high = mid - 1  # Try to find an earlier occurrence in the left half\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return first_idx\n\n    def _find_last_occurrence(arr, target, low, high):\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the last occurrence of the target using binary search.\"\"\"\n        last_idx = -1\n        while low <= high:\n            mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n            if arr[mid] == target:\n                last_idx = mid\n                low = mid + 1  # Try to find a later occurrence in the right half\n            elif arr[mid] < target:\n                low = mid + 1\n            else:\n                high = mid - 1\n        return last_idx\n\n    first_occurrence_idx = _find_first_occurrence(array, element, 0, n - 1)\n\n    # If the element is not found, it cannot be a majority element\n    if first_occurrence_idx == -1:\n        return False\n\n    last_occurrence_idx = _find_last_occurrence(array, element, 0, n - 1)\n\n    # Calculate the count of the element\n    count = last_occurrence_idx - first_occurrence_idx + 1\n\n    # Check if the count is greater than n/2\n    return count > (n // 2)"}
