{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def _calculate_even_bit_mask() -> int:\n    \"\"\"Generates a bitmask with 1s in all even positions (0, 2, 4, ...).\"\"\"\n    # This mask covers up to 128 bits, which is sufficient for most practical integers.\n    return 0x55555555555555555555555555555555\n\ndef _apply_bitwise_or(number: int, mask: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Applies a bitwise OR operation between the number and the mask.\"\"\"\n    return number | mask\n\ndef even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even-positioned bits (0, 2, 4, ...) of a given number to 1.\"\"\"\n    even_mask = _calculate_even_bit_mask()\n    result = _apply_bitwise_or(number, even_mask)\n    return result"}
