{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets bits at 0-indexed odd positions to 1, effectively setting 1-indexed even positions.\n    This interpretation satisfies the provided test case for input 10.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Helper function to generate a bitmask with 1s at odd 0-indexed positions\n    # (i.e., 1st, 3rd, 5th, etc., bits when counted from the right starting at 0).\n    # This corresponds to 1-indexed even positions (2nd, 4th, 6th, etc.).\n    # The mask's length is determined by the input number's bit length.\n    def _calculate_odd_positioned_bits_mask(bit_length: int) -> int:\n        mask = 0\n        for i in range(bit_length):\n            if i % 2 != 0:  # If the position (0-indexed) is odd\n                mask |= (1 << i)\n        return mask\n\n    # Determine the required bit length for the mask.\n    # For a number N, bit_length() returns the number of bits required to represent N\n    # in binary, excluding the sign and leading zeros.\n    # If the number is 0, bit_length() is 0, resulting in a mask of 0.\n    mask_bit_length = number.bit_length()\n\n    # Generate the mask with 1s at 0-indexed odd positions.\n    odd_positioned_mask = _calculate_odd_positioned_bits_mask(mask_bit_length)\n\n    # Apply a bitwise OR operation to set these bits in the original number.\n    return number | odd_positioned_mask"}
