{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def normalize_tuple(input_tuple: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Normalize tuple by sorting elements in ascending order.\n    This ensures that tuples with the same elements but different orders are considered equivalent.\n    \"\"\"\n    return tuple(sorted(input_tuple))\n\ndef check_occurences(tuple_list: list) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Count occurrences of tuples, treating different orders as equivalent.\n    Returns a dictionary mapping normalized tuples to their counts.\n    \"\"\"\n    counts = {}\n    for item_tuple in tuple_list:\n        normalized_item = normalize_tuple(item_tuple)\n        counts[normalized_item] = counts.get(normalized_item, 0) + 1\n    return counts"}
