{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "import math\n\ndef next_Perfect_Square(number: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the next perfect square strictly greater than the given number.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate the square root of the input number.\n    sqrt_val = math.sqrt(number)\n\n    # To find the next perfect square, we need the smallest integer 'k'\n    # such that k*k > number. This implies k > sqrt(number).\n    # The smallest integer k greater than sqrt(number) is floor(sqrt(number)) + 1.\n    next_integer_root = math.floor(sqrt_val) + 1\n\n    # Square this integer root to get the next perfect square.\n    result = next_integer_root * next_integer_root\n    \n    return result"}
