{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the length of the longest palindromic subsequence in the given string.\n    Uses dynamic programming with O(n^2) time and space complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of substring s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0 for _ in range(n)] for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All substrings of length 1 have an LPS length of 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table for lengths from 2 to n\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters match, add 2 to the LPS of the inner substring\n                # (dp[i+1][j-1] will be 0 if length is 2, correctly giving 2)\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + (dp[i+1][j-1] if length > 2 else 0)\n            else:\n                # If characters don't match, take the maximum of excluding s[i] or s[j]\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i+1][j], dp[i][j-1])\n\n    return dp[0][n-1]"}
