{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A bitonic subsequence is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n\n    # Handle edge cases for empty or single-element arrays.\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # Calculate LIS_sum: maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at each position.\n    # lis_sum[i] stores the max sum of an IS ending with arr[i].\n    lis_sum = list(arr) \n    for i in range(1, n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lis_sum[i] = max(lis_sum[i], lis_sum[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Calculate LDS_sum: maximum sum of a decreasing subsequence starting at each position.\n    # lds_sum[i] stores the max sum of a DS starting with arr[i].\n    lds_sum = list(arr)\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1): # Iterate backward from n-2 down to 0\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1): # Iterate backward from n-1 down to i+1\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                lds_sum[i] = max(lds_sum[i], lds_sum[j] + arr[i])\n\n    # Combine LIS_sum and LDS_sum to find the maximum bitonic sum.\n    # For each element arr[i] considered as the peak, the sum is lis_sum[i] + lds_sum[i] - arr[i].\n    # arr[i] is subtracted because it's included in both lis_sum[i] and lds_sum[i] calculations.\n    \n    # Initialize max_bitonic_sum with the sum for the first element, which is arr[0].\n    # (lis_sum[0] + lds_sum[0] - arr[0] simplifies to arr[0] + arr[0] - arr[0] = arr[0])\n    max_bitonic_sum = lis_sum[0] + lds_sum[0] - arr[0]\n    \n    for i in range(n):\n        max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, lis_sum[i] + lds_sum[i] - arr[i])\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
