{"task_id": "Mbpp/245", "solution": "def max_sum(array: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of a bitonic subsequence in the given array.\n    A sequence is bitonic if it is first increasing and then decreasing.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n\n    # A bitonic subsequence needs at least three elements to have distinct increasing and decreasing parts.\n    if n < 3:\n        return 0\n\n    # Calculate max increasing subsequence sum ending at each position.\n    inc_sums = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n):\n        inc_sums[i] = array[i]\n        for j in range(i):\n            if array[j] < array[i]:\n                inc_sums[i] = max(inc_sums[i], inc_sums[j] + array[i])\n\n    # Calculate max decreasing subsequence sum starting at each position.\n    dec_sums = [0] * n\n    for i in range(n - 1, -1, -1):\n        dec_sums[i] = array[i]\n        for j in range(n - 1, i, -1):\n            if array[j] < array[i]:\n                dec_sums[i] = max(dec_sums[i], dec_sums[j] + array[i])\n\n    # Combine increasing and decreasing sums to find the maximum bitonic sum.\n    max_bitonic_sum = 0\n    for i in range(n):\n        # For array[i] to be a peak of a valid bitonic subsequence, it must be part of an increasing\n        # sequence from its left AND a decreasing sequence to its right, both non-trivial.\n        if inc_sums[i] > array[i] and dec_sums[i] > array[i]:\n            current_bitonic_sum = inc_sums[i] + dec_sums[i] - array[i]\n            max_bitonic_sum = max(max_bitonic_sum, current_bitonic_sum)\n\n    return max_bitonic_sum"}
