{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of prime numbers less than the given non-negative number.\n    This function utilizes a helper function to determine primality.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_prime(n: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Determines if a given number is prime using trial division.\n        It efficiently checks for divisors up to the square root of n.\n        \"\"\"\n        if n < 2:\n            return False\n        if n == 2:\n            return True\n        if n % 2 == 0: # All other even numbers are not prime\n            return False\n        \n        # Check for odd factors from 3 up to sqrt(n)\n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= n:\n            if n % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    if number <= 2:\n        return 0 # There are no primes less than or equal to 2\n\n    count = 0\n    # Iterate through numbers from 2 up to (number - 1)\n    for i in range(2, number):\n        if _is_prime(i):\n            count += 1\n            \n    return count"}
