{"task_id": "Mbpp/285", "solution": "import re\n\ndef text_match_two_three(text: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a string contains the 'a' character followed by exactly two or three 'b' characters.\n    Uses regex for efficient and precise pattern matching.\n    \"\"\"\n    # The pattern 'a(bb|bbb)(?!b)' matches 'a' followed by 'bb' or 'bbb',\n    # and then ensures that this sequence is NOT followed by another 'b' (negative lookahead).\n    # This guarantees 'exactly two or three b's'.\n    pattern = r'a(bb|bbb)(?!b)'\n    return re.search(pattern, text) is not None"}
