{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list[int], n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous array in the modified array formed\n    by repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Handle edge cases for an empty array or no repetitions.\n    if n == 0 or k == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    def kadane_algorithm(local_arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Finds the maximum subarray sum using Kadane's algorithm, ensuring\n        at least the largest single element is returned if all are negative.\n        \"\"\"\n        # This function assumes local_arr is not empty, as outer function handles n=0.\n        max_so_far = local_arr[0]\n        current_max = local_arr[0]\n\n        for x in local_arr[1:]:\n            current_max = max(x, current_max + x)\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n        return max_so_far\n\n    # Calculate max sum for a single instance of the array.\n    max_sum_single = kadane_algorithm(arr)\n\n    # If k is 1, no repetition is needed, so return the single array's max sum.\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_sum_single\n\n    total_arr_sum = sum(arr)\n\n    # Calculate the maximum prefix sum, ensuring it includes at least one element.\n    max_prefix_sum = arr[0]\n    current_running_sum_prefix = arr[0]\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        current_running_sum_prefix += arr[i]\n        max_prefix_sum = max(max_prefix_sum, current_running_sum_prefix)\n\n    # Calculate the maximum suffix sum, ensuring it includes at least one element.\n    max_suffix_sum = arr[n - 1]\n    current_running_sum_suffix = arr[n - 1]\n    for i in range(n - 2, -1, -1):\n        current_running_sum_suffix += arr[i]\n        max_suffix_sum = max(max_suffix_sum, current_running_sum_suffix)\n\n    # Initialize overall maximum sum with what can be found in a single array.\n    overall_max_sum = max_sum_single\n\n    # Consider subarrays that span across the boundary of two repetitions.\n    # This involves a suffix of the first array and a prefix of the second.\n    overall_max_sum = max(overall_max_sum, max_prefix_sum + max_suffix_sum)\n\n    # If the total sum of the array is positive, and k > 1,\n    # the maximum sum might include (k-2) full array sums plus the best span across two arrays.\n    if total_arr_sum > 0:\n        overall_max_sum = max(overall_max_sum, total_arr_sum * (k - 2) + max_prefix_sum + max_suffix_sum)\n    \n    return overall_max_sum"}
