{"task_id": "Mbpp/296", "solution": "def get_Inv_Count(array: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Count the number of inversions in an array using a nested loop approach.\n\n    An inversion is a pair of indices (i, j) where i < j and array[i] > array[j].\n    \"\"\"\n    inversion_count = 0\n    n = len(array)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            if array[i] > array[j]:\n                inversion_count += 1\n    return inversion_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/294", "solution": "from typing import Union, List, Any\n\ndef _is_numeric(value: Any) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Check if a value is numeric (int or float).\"\"\"\n    return isinstance(value, (int, float))\n\ndef _filter_numeric_values(input_list: List[Any]) -> List[Union[int, float]]:\n    \"\"\"Filter and return only numeric values from the input list.\"\"\"\n    return [val for val in input_list if _is_numeric(val)]\n\ndef _find_maximum(numeric_values: List[Union[int, float]]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"Find and return the maximum value from a list of numeric values.\"\"\"\n    return max(numeric_values)\n\ndef max_val(input_list: List[Any]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the maximum numeric value in a heterogeneous list.\n    It filters for numeric types and then finds the maximum among them.\n    \"\"\"\n    numeric_items = _filter_numeric_values(input_list)\n    return _find_maximum(numeric_items)"}
