{"task_id": "Mbpp/306", "solution": "def max_sum_increasing_subseq(array: list[int], length: int, i: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence from the prefix until index i,\n    including the element at index k (where k > i).\n    \"\"\"\n\n    k_val = array[k]\n\n    # dp[x] stores the maximum sum of an increasing subsequence ending at array[x]\n    # within the prefix array[0...i].\n    dp = [0] * (i + 1)\n\n    # Initialize dp values with each element itself forming a subsequence.\n    for x in range(i + 1):\n        dp[x] = array[x]\n\n    # Compute maximum sum increasing subsequence for the prefix (0 to i) using dynamic programming.\n    for x in range(1, i + 1):\n        for y in range(x):\n            if array[x] > array[y]:\n                dp[x] = max(dp[x], dp[y] + array[x])\n\n    # The overall maximum sum must include k_val. Initialize with k_val in case no prefix\n    # element can precede it in an increasing subsequence.\n    max_total_sum = k_val\n\n    # Consider appending k_val to all valid increasing subsequences found in the prefix.\n    for j in range(i + 1):\n        if array[j] < k_val:\n            max_total_sum = max(max_total_sum, dp[j] + k_val)\n\n    return max_total_sum"}
