{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(integer: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets the leftmost unset bit in the binary representation of an integer.\"\"\"\n    # If the integer is 0, its leftmost unset bit is at position 0.\n    if integer == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Determine the position of the most significant bit.\n    # We will check bits from this position downwards.\n    msb_pos = integer.bit_length() - 1\n    \n    leftmost_unset_pos = -1\n\n    # Iterate from the MSB position down to 0 to find the first (leftmost) unset bit.\n    for pos in range(msb_pos, -1, -1):\n        # Check if the bit at 'pos' is 0 (unset).\n        if not (integer >> pos) & 1:\n            leftmost_unset_pos = pos\n            break\n    \n    # If no unset bit was found within the current bit_length (e.g., integer is 7 which is 0b111),\n    # then the leftmost unset bit is at the position immediately following the MSB.\n    if leftmost_unset_pos == -1:\n        leftmost_unset_pos = integer.bit_length()\n\n    # Set the identified leftmost unset bit using a bitwise OR operation.\n    return integer | (1 << leftmost_unset_pos)"}
