{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds a pair with the highest product from a given array of integers.\n    This implementation follows a design using helper functions for clarity.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _generate_pairs(arr):\n        \"\"\"Generates all unique pairs from the input array.\"\"\"\n        pairs = []\n        n = len(arr)\n        for i in range(n):\n            for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                pairs.append((arr[i], arr[j]))\n        return pairs\n\n    def _calculate_max_product_pair(pairs_list):\n        \"\"\"Calculates products and finds the pair with the maximum product.\"\"\"\n        max_prod = -float('inf')\n        max_pair_result = None\n\n        for p1, p2 in pairs_list:\n            current_prod = p1 * p2\n            if current_prod > max_prod:\n                max_prod = current_prod\n                max_pair_result = (p1, p2)\n        return max_pair_result\n    \n    all_possible_pairs = _generate_pairs(array)\n    \n    highest_product_pair = _calculate_max_product_pair(all_possible_pairs)\n    \n    return highest_product_pair"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(array: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the pair of numbers with the highest product from an array of integers.\"\"\"\n    n = len(array)\n    # Initialize with the product of the first two elements.\n    # This handles cases where all products might be negative.\n    max_product = array[0] * array[1]\n    max_pair = (array[0], array[1])\n\n    # Iterate through all possible pairs\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i + 1, n):\n            current_product = array[i] * array[j]\n            if current_product > max_product:\n                max_product = current_product\n                max_pair = (array[i], array[j])\n\n    return max_pair"}
