{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(arr: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum product of a contiguous subarray in the given array.\n    Uses a dynamic programming approach to track maximum and minimum products ending at the current position.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0  # Or handle as an error based on stricter requirements, but 0 for product is common.\n\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    min_so_far = arr[0]\n    result = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        curr = arr[i]\n\n        # If current number is negative, swap max_so_far and min_so_far\n        # because multiplying by a negative number flips the maximum and minimum\n        if curr < 0:\n            max_so_far, min_so_far = min_so_far, max_so_far\n\n        # Update max_so_far and min_so_far for the current position\n        max_so_far = max(curr, max_so_far * curr)\n        min_so_far = min(curr, min_so_far * curr)\n\n        # Update the global maximum result\n        result = max(result, max_so_far)\n\n    return result"}
