{"task_id": "Mbpp/472", "solution": "def check_Consecutive(numbers: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given list contains consecutive numbers.\n    The list must contain at least two numbers to form a consecutive sequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(numbers) < 2:\n        return False\n\n    # Sort the list to arrange numbers in ascending order, which is necessary\n    # for checking consecutiveness.\n    numbers.sort()\n\n    # Iterate through the sorted list, starting from the second element,\n    # and verify if each number is exactly one greater than its predecessor.\n    for i in range(1, len(numbers)):\n        if numbers[i] - numbers[i-1] != 1:\n            return False\n\n    # If the loop completes without finding any non-consecutive pairs,\n    # the numbers in the list are consecutive.\n    return True"}
