{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "def normalize_tuple(t: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts elements within a tuple to enable order-independent comparison.\n    Returns a new tuple with elements sorted.\n    \"\"\"\n    return tuple(sorted(t))\n\ndef find_matches(normalized_list1: list, normalized_list2: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds common normalized tuples between two lists of normalized tuples.\n    Returns a list of these common normalized tuples.\n    \"\"\"\n    set1 = set(normalized_list1)\n    set2 = set(normalized_list2)\n    return list(set1.intersection(set2))\n\ndef create_result_set(common_normalized_tuples: list, original_list1: list) -> set:\n    \"\"\"\n    Creates a set of original tuples from common normalized tuples, prioritizing list1's representation.\n    Iterates through original_list1 to find matching tuples based on their normalized form.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = set()\n    common_norm_set = set(common_normalized_tuples)\n\n    for original_t in original_list1:\n        if normalize_tuple(original_t) in common_norm_set:\n            result.add(original_t)\n    return result\n\ndef tuple_intersection(list1: list, list2: list) -> set:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the intersection of tuples from two lists, irrespective of element order within tuples.\n    The result set contains tuples using the representation found in the first input list.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Normalize all tuples in both lists for comparison\n    normalized_list1 = [normalize_tuple(t) for t in list1]\n    normalized_list2 = [normalize_tuple(t) for t in list2]\n\n    # Find the common normalized tuples\n    common_normalized_tuples = find_matches(normalized_list1, normalized_list2)\n\n    # Create the final result set using original tuples from list1 that correspond to the common normalized tuples\n    return create_result_set(common_normalized_tuples, list1)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/475", "solution": "import collections\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Tuple, Union\n\ndef sort_counter(input_dict: Dict[str, Union[int, float]]) -> List[Tuple[str, Union[int, float]]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a dictionary by its values in descending order.\n    Returns a list of tuples sorted by value.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Convert the dictionary items to a list of (key, value) tuples.\n    # Sort the list using the 'sorted' function, specifying the key for sorting\n    # as the second element of each tuple (the value), and in reverse order.\n    return sorted(input_dict.items(), key=lambda item: item[1], reverse=True)"}
