{"task_id": "Mbpp/602", "solution": "def first_repeated_char(input_string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first character that appears more than once in the input string.\n    Scans the string from left to right to identify the first repeated character.\n    \"\"\"\n    seen_chars = set()\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char in seen_chars:\n            return char\n        seen_chars.add(char)\n    # The problem implies a repeated character will always be found for valid inputs.\n    # If no character repeats, the function would implicitly return None, but this path\n    # is not expected for the problem constraints."}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/602", "solution": "def first_repeated_char(input_string: str) -> str | None:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the first repeated character in a string.\n    This function orchestrates helpers to track character positions and identify the earliest repeating character.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _track_character_positions(input_string: str) -> dict[str, list[int]]:\n        \"\"\"Track all positions of each character in the string.\"\"\"\n        char_positions = {}\n        for i, char in enumerate(input_string):\n            if char not in char_positions:\n                char_positions[char] = []\n            char_positions[char].append(i)\n        return char_positions\n\n    def _find_first_repeated(char_positions: dict[str, list[int]]) -> str | None:\n        \"\"\"Identify the character whose second occurrence appears earliest in the string.\"\"\"\n        first_repeat_char_candidate = None\n        min_second_occurrence_index = float('inf')\n\n        for char, positions in char_positions.items():\n            if len(positions) > 1:  # This character is repeated at least once\n                # The second occurrence's index determines which character \"repeats first\"\n                if positions[1] < min_second_occurrence_index:\n                    min_second_occurrence_index = positions[1]\n                    first_repeat_char_candidate = char\n        return first_repeat_char_candidate\n\n    if not input_string:\n        return None\n\n    tracked_positions = _track_character_positions(input_string)\n    result = _find_first_repeated(tracked_positions)\n    return result"}
