{"task_id": "Mbpp/731", "solution": "import math\n\ndef lateralsurface_cone(r, h):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the lateral surface area of a cone given its radius and height.\n    The formula used is pi * r * sqrt(r^2 + h^2).\n    \"\"\"\n    slant_height = math.sqrt(r**2 + h**2)\n    lateral_surface_area = math.pi * r * slant_height\n    return lateral_surface_area"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/731", "solution": "import math\n\ndef lateralsurface_cone(r, h):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the lateral surface area of a cone given its radius and height.\n    Uses the formula: \u03c0 * r * \u221a(r\u00b2 + h\u00b2).\n    \"\"\"\n    slant_height = math.sqrt(math.pow(r, 2) + math.pow(h, 2))\n    lateral_surface_area = math.pi * r * slant_height\n    return lateral_surface_area"}
