{"task_id": "Mbpp/736", "solution": "def left_insertion(array: list[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Find the leftmost insertion point for target in sorted array.\n\n    Args:\n        array: Sorted list of integers\n        target: Integer value to find insertion point for\n\n    Returns:\n        Integer index where target should be inserted\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if array[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid\n    return low"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "def find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with n digits.\n    A triangular number is calculated as k * (k + 1) / 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    k = 1\n    while True:\n        triangular_number = k * (k + 1) // 2\n        # Count the number of digits in the triangular_number\n        num_digits = len(str(triangular_number))\n        \n        if num_digits == n:\n            return k\n        \n        k += 1"}
