{"task_id": "Mbpp/740", "solution": "def tuple_to_dict(input_tuple: tuple) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a tuple to a key-value dictionary using adjacent elements.\n    Odd-indexed elements become keys, even-indexed elements become values.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_dict = {}\n    for i in range(0, len(input_tuple), 2):\n        if i + 1 < len(input_tuple):\n            result_dict[input_tuple[i]] = input_tuple[i+1]\n    return result_dict"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "def find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the smallest triangular number with n digits.\n    Iterates through triangular numbers, checking their digit count.\n    \"\"\"\n    def calculate_triangular_number(index: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the triangular number for a given index.\"\"\"\n        return index * (index + 1) // 2\n\n    def count_digits(number: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Counts the number of digits in an integer.\"\"\"\n        return len(str(number))\n\n    index = 1\n    while True:\n        triangular_num = calculate_triangular_number(index)\n        digits = count_digits(triangular_num)\n        if digits == n:\n            return index\n        index += 1"}
