{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, rotation_count: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotate a list to the right by specified number of positions.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: List to be rotated\n        rotation_count: Number of positions to rotate right\n\n    Returns:\n        New list with elements rotated to the right\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    list_length = len(input_list)\n    effective_rotation = rotation_count % list_length\n\n    # Slice the list into two parts:\n    # 1. The last 'effective_rotation' elements (which move to the front)\n    # 2. The remaining elements (which follow the first part)\n    rotated_part = input_list[list_length - effective_rotation:]\n    remaining_part = input_list[:list_length - effective_rotation]\n\n    return rotated_part + remaining_part"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(lst: list, positions: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items, returning a new list.\n    The original list remains unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not lst:\n        return []\n\n    n = len(lst)\n    effective_positions = positions % n\n\n    if effective_positions == 0:\n        return list(lst)  # Return a copy if no rotation needed\n\n    # Split the list into two parts: the end part that moves to the front, and the beginning part\n    rotated_part = lst[-effective_positions:]\n    remaining_part = lst[:-effective_positions]\n\n    return rotated_part + remaining_part"}
