{"task_id": "Mbpp/766", "solution": "def pair_wise(input_list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a list of all consecutive pairs from the input list.\n    Each pair is represented as a tuple (item, next_item).\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    pairs = []\n    # Iterate up to the second-to-last item to ensure a successor exists\n    for i in range(len(input_list) - 1):\n        pairs.append((input_list[i], input_list[i+1]))\n    return pairs"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "def is_polite(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the nth polite number.\n    A polite number is a positive integer that is not a power of 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    polite_count = 0\n    current_num = 1\n\n    while polite_count < n:\n        # A positive integer is a power of 2 if (num > 0 and (num & (num - 1)) == 0).\n        # Since current_num starts at 1 and increases, it is always positive.\n        if (current_num & (current_num - 1)) != 0:\n            # If it's not a power of 2, it's a polite number.\n            polite_count += 1\n\n        # If the current number is the nth polite number, return it.\n        if polite_count == n:\n            return current_num\n\n        current_num += 1"}
