{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, distance: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotate left bits by d bits for a 32-bit number.\n\n    Args:\n        number: 32-bit integer to rotate\n        distance: Number of positions to rotate left\n\n    Returns:\n        int: Result of left bit rotation\n    \"\"\"\n    BITS = 32\n    # Normalize the rotation distance\n    d = distance % BITS\n\n    # Calculate the left-shifted part of the number\n    shifted_left = number << d\n\n    # Calculate the bits that wrap around from the left to the right\n    shifted_right = number >> (BITS - d)\n\n    # Combine the two parts\n    rotated_result = shifted_left | shifted_right\n\n    # Mask the result to keep it within 32 bits\n    return rotated_result & 0xFFFFFFFF"}
