{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotate the bits of a 32-bit integer to the left by d positions.\n\n    Args:\n        number: 32-bit integer to rotate\n        d: number of positions to rotate left\n\n    Returns:\n        32-bit integer with bits rotated left\n    \"\"\"\n    # Normalize the rotation count to be within 0-31\n    d %= 32\n\n    # Perform the left rotation\n    # (number << d) shifts bits to the left\n    # (number >> (32 - d)) captures the bits that wrap around from the left\n    rotated_number = (number << d) | (number >> (32 - d))\n\n    # Mask the result to ensure it remains a 32-bit integer\n    return rotated_number & 0xFFFFFFFF"}
