{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "import math\n\ndef is_perfect_square(number: [int, float]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is a perfect square.\n    Returns True if it is, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n    \n    # Calculate the square root using math.sqrt\n    sqrt_val = math.sqrt(number)\n    \n    # A number is a perfect square if its square root is an integer.\n    # Compare the square root value to its integer representation.\n    return sqrt_val == int(sqrt_val)"}
